.TH FINANCE-RECEIPT-MATCH 1 "2026-11-10" "Finance Infrastructure" "Nexus Host Utilities"
.SH NAME
finance-receipt-match \- stage one-to-one receipt and bank spending candidates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /opt/data/bin/finance-receipt-match
.RB [ --preview | --apply ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads validated, non-duplicate CAD purchase receipts from the existing
finance-analytics PostgreSQL and Wealthfolio activities through the existing
read-scoped Receipt Wrangler MCP credential. A candidate requires a CAD
WITHDRAWAL with exactly the receipt total, a posting date within three days,
strong normalized merchant agreement, and unique receipt and activity ownership.
Ambiguous or unmatched receipts are not linked. Existing non-candidate links are
preserved; drift in candidate links or bank snapshots stops the run.
.PP
The default
.B --preview
only reports aggregate candidates. With
.B --apply
it atomically inserts candidate-only rows into the existing
.B bank_activity_snapshot
and
.B receipt_transaction_matches
tables. Each activity and receipt has a unique key; repeated runs add no rows.
The snapshot spending view is a partial, candidate-linked subset, not a complete
bank ledger or a valid budget. The matcher never creates Wealthfolio expenses,
confirms receipt ownership, or changes Receipt Wrangler or Proton email.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Host Python 3.9+, Docker/psql, systemd-creds, bws,
.B /usr/local/sbin/receipt-match-audit
for its native MCP client, the existing Bitwarden
.B WEALTHFOLIO_RECEIPT_MATCH_READ
secret, local Wealthfolio, and finance-analytics PostgreSQL. Before applying,
verify a protected finance-analytics backup and its second-host copy.
.SH OUTPUT
Only aggregate counts and generic error types. Exit nonzero means stop and
review the exact protected database state; never infer a failed write was rolled
back. The existing finance-intake systemd oneshot invokes this after receipt
projection and authenticated mail staging.
.SH ROLLBACK
Inspect the exact candidate receipt/activity IDs, any owner confirmations or
later dependencies, then delete only eligible candidate match rows and their
orphaned snapshot rows transactionally. Never remove confirmed links or restore
a whole live database over intervening owner writes. Git owns the executable,
unit, and this manual.
